# ============================================================
#  Quadis Hotels FRONTEND — build-time configuration
# ============================================================
#  Copy to .env (or .env.production) before running `npm run build`.
#  Vite inlines these at BUILD time, not runtime — changing one means
#  rebuilding and re-uploading the bundle.
#
#  The backend has its own separate file: backend/.env.example
# ============================================================

# ── API origin (REQUIRED in production) ─────────────────────
# Absolute URL of the API, including the /api path.
#
# Leave this unset ONLY if something is routing /api/* on this domain through
# to the backend (a CloudFront behaviour, an nginx proxy, Render rewrites).
# On a plain S3 static site nothing does, so every API call returns the SPA's
# index.html — and because the hotels list falls back to bundled static data,
# the site *looks* fine while registration, sign-in, enquiry forms, bookings
# and payments are all silently dead.
#
# Examples:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.quadishotels.com/api
#   VITE_API_URL=https://quadis-backend.onrender.com/api
VITE_API_URL=

# Local development needs nothing here: any localhost/127.0.0.1 origin
# automatically targets http://localhost:3001/api.
